{"name":"Strawberry Shortcake","hex":"#fa8e99","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"strawberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sweet, usually red, edible accessory fruit of certain plants of the genus Fragaria.","Any plant of the genus Fragaria (that bears such fruit)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavor of strawberries.","Flavored with ethyl methylphenylglycidate, an artificial compound which is said to resemble the taste of strawberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strawberry"},{"term":"shortcake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet cake or biscuit (crumbly leavened bread) typically made with flour, sugar, salt, butter, milk or cream, and sometimes eggs, and leavened with baking powder or baking soda.","A dessert made with such a cake, typically having layers of cream and fruit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shortcake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Strawberry shortcake (dessert)","blocks":[{"text":"Strawberry shortcake is an American dessert made with strawberries that have been sliced or macerated, sweetened cream or whipped cream, and either shortcake or sponge cake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Stawberry_shortcake.jpeg/330px-Stawberry_shortcake.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry_shortcake_(dessert)","wikidata":"Q140502537"},{"title":"Strawberry Shortcake","blocks":[{"text":"Strawberry Shortcake is a media franchise that originated from a series of greeting cards published by American Greetings bearing the image of the titular character. The line was later expanded to include dolls, clothing, posters, and other products featuring the character, as well as an extended cast of friends and pets. In addition, the franchise has spawned television specials, animated television series and films. The franchise is currently owned by the Canadian children's television company WildBrain through the holding company Shortcake IP Holdings LLC."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e3/Strawberry-ShortcakeLife-is-Delicious-Poster-C10314364.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry_Shortcake","wikidata":"Q990035"},{"title":"Strawberry Shortcake (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Strawberry Shortcake is an American children's musical preschool animated series produced by DIC Entertainment and American Greetings based on the franchise of the same name that premiered on March 11, 2003. The series consists of 45 episodes, plus one short and one feature film based on this incarnation. The series was broadcast on television by CBS, HBO, HBO Family, and in broadcast syndication. The entire cast is replaced with younger and lesser known voice actors compared to the 1980s Strawberry Shortcake animated specials."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/ff/Strawberry_Shortcake_2003_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry_Shortcake_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q625671"},{"title":"Strawberry","blocks":[{"text":"The garden strawberry is a widely grown hybrid plant cultivated worldwide for its fruit. The genus Fragaria, the strawberries, is in the rose family, Rosaceae. The fruit is appreciated for its aroma, bright red colour, juicy texture, and sweetness. It is eaten either fresh or in prepared foods such as jam, ice cream, and chocolates. Artificial strawberry flavourings and aromas are widely used in commercial products. Botanically, the strawberry is not a berry, but an aggregate accessory fruit. Each apparent 'seed' on the outside of the strawberry is actually an achene, a botanical fruit with a seed inside it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg/330px-Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry","wikidata":"Q13158"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Strawberry_shortcake_from_Gibson%27s_Steakhouse_in_Chicago%2C_Illinois.jpg/500px-Strawberry_shortcake_from_Gibson%27s_Steakhouse_in_Chicago%2C_Illinois.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Strawberry_shortcake_from_Gibson%27s_Steakhouse_in_Chicago%2C_Illinois.jpg/500px-Strawberry_shortcake_from_Gibson%27s_Steakhouse_in_Chicago%2C_Illinois.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Strawberry shortcake from Gibson's Steakhouse in Chicago, Illinois","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStrawberry_shortcake_from_Gibson's_Steakhouse_in_Chicago%2C_Illinois.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Strawberry_Shortcake_%2813917733299%29.jpg/120px-Strawberry_Shortcake_%2813917733299%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Strawberry_Shortcake_%2813917733299%29.jpg/250px-Strawberry_Shortcake_%2813917733299%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Strawberry_Shortcake_%2813917733299%29.jpg/120px-Strawberry_Shortcake_%2813917733299%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStrawberry_Shortcake_(13917733299).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Strawberry_shortcake_with_whipcream.jpg/120px-Strawberry_shortcake_with_whipcream.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki